// texCoords2D tells the hardware whether TEXCOORDn interpolates as 2D.
// The rule, measured against the reference compiler over every corpus
// shader both compilers build:
//
//   bit n is CLEARED iff TEXCOORDn is READ and DECLARED wider than float2
//
// It is a property of the DECLARATION, not of the lanes a shader happens to
// consume: sd_tex_ctrl declares float4 TEXCOORD0, reads only .xy through an
// ordinary non-projective tex2D, and the reference clears the bit anyway.
// A rule keyed on consumed lanes gets that backwards.
//
// One TEXCOORD per case, so a fix cannot pass by clearing too broadly or
// too narrowly:
//   TEXCOORD0  wide AND read   -> CLEARED
//   TEXCOORD1  float2 and read -> SET   (clearing this is over-broad)
//   TEXCOORD2  wide, NOT read  -> SET   (an unread varying is not
//                                        interpolated, so its bit stays)
//   TEX3       wide AND read   -> CLEARED
//   TEXCOORD4  wide, read ONLY as a tex2D coordinate -> CLEARED
//
// TEXCOORD4 is the sd_tex_ctrl shape and it is the case that discriminates
// the two candidate rules.  Under "clear when the read needs more than xy"
// it stays SET, because tex2D consumes only .xy; under the declared-width
// rule it CLEARS, which is what the reference does.  The general path used
// to clear on `op != Tex && !scalarYRead`, so it got TEXCOORD0 right (read
// by an add) and this one wrong - a fixture without this case passes on a
// build where only the default path is fixed.
//
// TEX3 is the same semantic as TEXCOORD3: fragmentInputSrc accepts both
// spellings and the parser keeps it as name "TEX" with index 3.  The first
// version of this fixture used only the TEXCOORD spelling, and the fix it
// guarded matched only that string - so a shader written with TEX had its
// read mask set and its declared width missed, and the bit stayed set
// (review finding, codex).
void main(float4 wideRead   : TEXCOORD0,
          float2 narrowRead : TEXCOORD1,
          float4 wideUnread : TEXCOORD2,
          float4 aliasRead  : TEX3,
          float4 wideTexOnly : TEXCOORD4,
          uniform sampler2D tex,
          out float4 color : COLOR)
{
    color = tex2D(tex, narrowRead) + wideRead + aliasRead
          + tex2D(tex, wideTexOnly.xy);
}
